title: Order storage decisions
description: Decision records next to what they decide; a newer decision supersedes an older one.

adr db: Use Postgres for orders [accepted] {
  context: Orders and payments change together and must stay consistent; reporting needs ad-hoc queries.
  options: Postgres (RDS), DynamoDB, MongoDB Atlas
  decision: Postgres on RDS, one schema per service.
  consequences: Migrations become part of every release. No single-table design; joins are fine.
}
adr cache: Cache order reads in Redis [proposed] {
  context: The order page reads the same order many times a minute.
  options: Redis, read replicas, no cache
  decision: Redis with a 60s TTL, invalidated on write.
  consequences: One more service to run; stale reads for up to a minute.
}
adr mongo: Store orders in MongoDB [superseded] {
  context: Early prototype, schema still moving.
  decision: MongoDB Atlas.
}

db -> mongo: supersedes
